<div class="organization-tfa-notice">
<h1>Organization two-factor authentication</h1>
<p><strong><%= @organization.name %></strong> requires two-factor authentication from <strong><%= DateTime.to_iso8601(@organization.tfa_required_at) %> (UTC)</strong>.</p>
<%= if @stage == "summary" do %><p>Members suspended because 2FA isn't enabled: <%= if @suspended == [], do: "none", else: Enum.join(@suspended, ", ") %>.</p><% end %>
<%= if @stage == "suspended" do %><p>Your organization access is suspended until you enable 2FA. Your membership, role, package ownership, and billed seat are retained.</p><% end %>
<p>Enable 2FA in your <a href="<%= email_url("/dashboard/security") %>">account security settings</a> and authenticate your Hex client. Personal API keys, tokens exchanged from them, and password-only API access won't work for this organization after enforcement starts, even if 2FA is enabled on your account. Use organization-owned credentials for automation.</p>
<p>Verify 2FA every <%= if @organization.tfa_session_lifetime_seconds == 86400, do: "24 hours", else: "#{div(@organization.tfa_session_lifetime_seconds, 86400)} days" %>. SSO authentication is separate and may also be required. Recovery codes remain available. After enrollment, return to any pending invitation to accept it.
</p>
</div>
